<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Fury Warriors</span></h2>Crafted items from Blacksmithing are not restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Blacksmith, you can equip anything Blacksmiths craft. Early on, these crafted items will be very powerful, but also expensive.<div data-inserted-ad-group="1" style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; justify-content: center; align-items: center;">
<div data-ad="inline-leaderboard" id="ad_inline-leaderboard_1" style="width: 728px; height: 90px; background: rgba(136, 136, 136, 0.133); --ad-width: 728px; --ad-height: 90px;"></div></div>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is the best-crafted item available in Mists of Pandaria Phase 1. If you can only purchase one crafted item, this trinket should be your choice, as it remains BiS throughout the entire phase.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> is restricted to Engineers, and is a powerful 476 item level option. It has 2 cogwheel sockets, which allow you to gem a specific engineering cogwheel gem, like for example <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77543/precise-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Precise Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Tinker's Gear</span></a>, which provides 600 secondary stat instead of 320.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a> is a powerful 496 item level option crafted by Blacksmiths. It's important to note that this item is not craftable prior to the release of Mogu'shan Vautls.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87402/ornate-battleplate-of-the-master">
<img alt="Ornate Battleplate of the Master" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ornate Battleplate of the Master</span></a> is another powerful 496 item level option crafted by Blacksmiths. It's important to note that item is also not craftable prior to the release of Mogu'shan Vautls.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82975/ghost-reavers-breastplate">
<img alt="Ghost Reaver's Breastplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Reaver's Breastplate</span></a> is a strong 476 item level option crafted by Blacksmiths.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82976/ghost-reavers-gauntlets">
<img alt="Ghost Reaver's Gauntlets" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_plate_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Reaver's Gauntlets</span></a> is another strong 476 item level option crafted by Blacksmiths.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Fury Warrior Trinkets</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Warriors should typically use one on-use and one passive trinket, or two passive trinkets, but rarely ever two on-use.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81268/lessons-of-the-darkmaster">
<img alt="Lessons of the Darkmaster" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lessons of the Darkmaster</span></a> is the only notable on-use trinket in Phase 1 pre-bis. The trinket provides a baseline amount of Expertise, and the on-use effect is a solid Strength bonus. This trinket on paper is worse than all the proc trinkets listed below. However, in certain situations where you want to time your damage, like in AoE or other damage amplification windows, this trinket can provide immense value.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is the best trinket option for Fury Warriors in Phase 1 pre-bis. It offers a strong 15-second Strength proc and a strong baseline Strength value. Relic of Xuen has a 20% proc chance from melee attacks and a 55-second internal cooldown. Keep in mind that this bind-on-equip trinket is likely to be very expensive early in Mists of Pandaria due to high demand and the fact that it can only be crafted through the Inscription profession.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81138/carbonic-carbuncle">
<img alt="Carbonic Carbuncle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Carbonic Carbuncle</span></a> is Fury Warriors second-best option in Phase 1 pre-bis. It offers a solid 30-second Critical Strike proc and a solid amount of Strength baseline. The trinket has a 15% chance to proc from attacks and has a 115-second internal cooldown.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> is the third-best trinket option in Phase 1 pre-bis. This Alchemy-specific trinket offers a large amount of Strength when procced, and has mastery baseline, which can be reforged into Critical Strike. It has a 25% chance to proc each time you deal damage, and has an internal cooldown of 55 seconds.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86802/lei-shens-final-orders">
<img alt="Lei Shen's Final Orders" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen's Final Orders</span></a> is the fourth-best trinket option in Phase 1 pre-bis. It's important to note that this trinket will only become attainable 2 weeks after Mogu'shan Vaults release. This trinket offers a strong Strength proc, and a solid baseline amount of Haste, which can be reforged into Critical Strike. It has a 15% chance to proc from attacks and has a 55-second internal cooldown.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Fury Warriors</span></h2>Fury Warrior gemming in Mist of Pandaria revolves primarily around being able to gem as much Critical Strike Rating as possible. The gem providing the greatest Critical Strike rating is <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76697/smooth-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Smooth Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Smooth Sun's Radiance</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>However, always consider socket bonuses when gemming. 1 Critical Strike Rating equates to about 1.07 Strength for Fury warriors. In scenarios when you want to reach socket bonuses, due to the socket bonus yielding enough value, you gem red sockets with <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76661/inscribed-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Inscribed Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Vermilion Onyx</span></a>, and blue sockets with <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76641/piercing-wild-jade">
<img alt="Piercing Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Piercing Wild Jade</span></a>. You may also gem <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76636/rigid-rivers-heart">
<img alt="Rigid River's Heart" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_blue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid River's Heart</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76693/precise-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Precise Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Primordial Ruby</span></a> in their respective sockets if you are struggling to reach Hit and Expertise cap.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76886/reverberating-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c4">Yellow Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76697/smooth-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Smooth Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Smooth Sun's Radiance</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76661/inscribed-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Inscribed Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c3">Green Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76641/piercing-wild-jade">
<img alt="Piercing Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Piercing Wild Jade</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76693/precise-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Precise Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c7">Blue Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76636/rigid-rivers-heart">
<img alt="Rigid River's Heart" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_blue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid River's Heart</span></a></div></li></ul>Once you start reaching about 490-500 overall item level, you will instead shift your gemming towards Critical Strike rather than Strength, due to sufficient AP values being reached. If you want to find out if you should start gemming Critical Strike over Strength, I recommend you input your gear into the Wowsims website and generate stat weights.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Fury Warriors</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that certain racials such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_orc_female.gif");'></span> Orc Racial <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=20574/axe-specialization">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Axe Specialization</span></a> will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This effectively means your abilities will never miss, though your regular swings still might.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, Raid bosses will no longer be able to Dodge your attacks. They will however still be able to Parry them, so make sure to position yourself behind mobs.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<hr/>Our fury warrior guides are always updated with the latest information from in-game experience, simulations, and logs; make sure to check our changelog to this page by clicking on <b>View Changelog</b> at the top of the page.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<hr/>
<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="feedback">Feedback</h2>Thanks for reading our class guides! If you have any feedback about the guides, feel free to leave a comment in the section below, and we will reply as quickly as possible. If you'd like to talk with any of our writers directly, you can do so by joining our <a data-contiguous="true" href="http://discord.gg/wowhead" target="_blank">Discord Server</a> and finding them there!<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
